{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Validate Code Generation",
  "description": "On save of a backend/frontend source file, review it against the project's TypeScript, OOP/SOLID, architecture, and error-handling steering, and confirm it type-checks.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "backend/src/**/*.ts",
      "frontend/src/**/*.ts",
      "frontend/src/**/*.tsx"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A source file was just saved. Validate ONLY that file against the workspace steering (typescript-best-practices, oop-compliance, architecture, error-handling, domain-modelling, validation). Check specifically:\n1. No `any` in domain/service/repository/store code; external data is treated as `unknown` and narrowed (no `as` on untrusted input). No `@ts-ignore`/`@ts-expect-error` outside tests.\n2. Layering respected: no SQL or snake_case/row types outside backend/src/db/; no business logic in route handlers; concrete classes constructed only in server.ts (Dependency Inversion via interfaces).\n3. Domain objects handled as Readonly and not mutated in place; DTOs derived via Omit/Partial/Pick; fixed value sets are const-object unions, not enums.\n4. Errors are typed (AppError/ApiError), never untyped throws; a failed mutation must not mutate client state.\n5. Run `npx tsc --noEmit` in the affected package and confirm it is clean.\nReport a short PASS/FAIL checklist. For any FAIL, name the exact line and the minimal fix. Do NOT rewrite unrelated code. If everything passes, say so in one line."
  }
}
